direction: right

title: |md
  ## Hash vs LPM: pick by lookup pattern
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

hash: "BPF_MAP_TYPE_HASH" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  h_body: |md
    Use when keys are **exact match**:
    - {tcp_flow_5tuple} → state
    - {pid} → counter
    - {socket_cookie} → metadata

    Lookup: O(1) hash + bucket walk
    Memory: O(N) entries

    **Cannot** match prefixes.
  |
}

lpm: "BPF_MAP_TYPE_LPM_TRIE" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  l_body: |md
    Use when keys are **prefixes**:
    - {prefixlen=24, 192.168.1.0} → action
    - {prefixlen=64, IPv6 net} → action

    Lookup: O(prefix_len) bit walk
    Memory: O(N + total_bits) for tree nodes

    **Returns longest matching prefix.**
    Per IPv4: max 32 hops; usually < 5
    Per IPv6: max 128 hops; usually < 16
  |
}

key_struct: "Key struct for LPM:" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  ks_body: |md
    ```c
    struct ipv4_key {
        __u32 prefixlen;     // ALWAYS first — kernel reads this
        __u32 addr;          // big-endian network address
    };
    ```
  |
}

hash -> key_struct: "exact-match keys" {style.stroke-dash: 4}
lpm -> key_struct: "prefix + value keys" {style.stroke-dash: 4}
